# GodsEye - what does not belong in the repository.
#
# Three separate reasons things are listed here: they are regenerable, they are
# too large for a git host, or they must not be redistributed. Each block says
# which, because "why is this ignored" is the question someone asks a year
# later when a clone does not run.

# --- virtualenvs: machine-specific, and 2 GB -----------------------------
# .venv-paddle carries a full paddle + torch stack built against this machine's
# interpreter. It cannot be moved to another machine even if it were committed.
# PADDLE_SETUP.md is how it gets rebuilt.
.venv-paddle/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- python build artefacts ---------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- runtime state and secrets ------------------------------------------
# judge_token.txt is the shared secret that protects the public judge link.
# Committing it would publish the one thing that makes the tunnel safe to
# share, and it is recreated automatically on first use.
data/judge_token.txt
data/tunnel_url.txt
data/tunnel.log

# phonecam/certs/ holds a TLS PRIVATE KEY. It is generated per machine by
# phonecam/certs.py - reissued automatically whenever this laptop's LAN address
# changes - so committing it would publish a private key to gain nothing.
phonecam/certs/

# Printable demo boards, regenerated by `python -m livecam.makeboard`.
livecam/boards/

# The sighting store is generated: `python seed.py` rebuilds ~6 h of city
# traffic in about a minute. It is also 57 MB and changes on every run, which
# is the worst possible shape for git.
data/godseye.db
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# ... and any scratch store left anywhere in the tree. The rule above named one
# path, so a control database seeded to compare a change against - test84.db,
# ctl168.db - sat outside it and was staged for commit by `git add -A`. A
# sighting store is never source, wherever it was written.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- model weights ------------------------------------------------------
# The three shipped models (crnn.pt, glyph_mlp.joblib, yolov8n-obb-plate.pt)
# ARE committed - they are a few MB each and RUN.md is explicit that a clone
# without them silently retrains and degrades.
#
# model.safetensors is different: 142 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, and
# anpr/anpr_ocr_reader.py downloads it from Hugging Face on first use anyway.
models/anpr_ocr/model.safetensors
models/anpr_ocr/.cache/
# A git clone of PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR, fetched automatically by
# _ensure_paddleocr(). Someone else's repository; not ours to carry.
models/anpr_ocr/PaddleOCR/

# --- third-party datasets: LICENCE RESTRICTED ---------------------------
# Ignored by default, deliberately. See the licence note at the end of RUN.md.
#
#   indian-number-plates-dataset/  CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. Non-commercial, attribution
#                                  required, and NO distribution of modified
#                                  versions. Republishing it - especially to a
#                                  public repository - is a licence breach.
#   dataset_v1_bbox/               A Roboflow export under its own licence; see
#                                  its README.roboflow.txt before sharing it.
#
# They are also 149 MB and 49 MB. Keep them alongside a clone rather than
# inside one.
indian-number-plates-dataset/
dataset_v1_bbox/

# --- editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- stale backups ------------------------------------------------------
*.bak

# --- design-session scratch and local DB snapshots ----------------------
# .impeccable/ keeps the design contract (design.json, surfaces/); its
# question logs and review screenshots are session scratch.
.impeccable/questions/
.impeccable/review/
data/*.bak-*

# real-photo evaluation corpus: CC BY-NC-ND derived and real registrations, private repo only
real_plate_crops/
real_plate_frame_labels.json
real_plate_transcriptions.json
real_plate_crops_manifest.txt
cluster_manifest.json
tools_fieldtest/
